Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraCircle", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"db7694ce-2ace-413e-822e-8a64066629e6"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraCircle"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCircle", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa9be62d-7a50-4b9a-aa4c-19f71e5f9c6f"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the family of circles around ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " at radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 ". It is inert; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c75975c4-6b94-493c-87e5-0347266acaaa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraRepresentative"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraRepresentative", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9a8e789a-a579-41af-bbe2-ec285b9eeeb6"],
 " evaluate it on a graph.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"84b99403-bfce-4c65-95ab-928b8002dc77"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraCircle"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCircle", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2793a177-ebf8-4a06-a55d-b47f2494b915"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the family in the band ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["d(c, v)", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 "; a scalar ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " means ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "r"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aea7d9ed-bb44-4f64-86ec-7475be641097"],
 ".",
 "\n",
 "The same expression inside an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraScene"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraScene", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "18388576-ed99-433b-b18f-b71957727d5a"],
 " is the circle construction token."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"9f3b9e95-1c2d-4c27-8a4f-99147e6b3d56"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: a circle of the band ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " around ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " is a shortest cycle of the subgraph induced on ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " whose removal leaves ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " in a component that reaches no further than the band."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0aa12ac1-64fa-460d-be0f-1543d57f8fd5"],

Cell["\<\
The second argument is always a radius or a band, never a point, so a vertex \
label that is an integer or a pair cannot be mistaken for one. There are no \
options.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"33ec3fbb-712e-4f25-bc9d-9d903c42d982"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Euclid's third postulate describes a circle with any centre and distance: \
the circle is named by its radius. The circle through a point ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is drawn by a compass opened to ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ", an arc that closes: it is the closed arc ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraArc"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraArc", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ab2aa33-eaad-4283-9349-a74e0b2c8e56"],
 ", the circles of the band of ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " that pass through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"deb3820d-552e-4752-a41d-1bf7f4729304"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A circle need not exist.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " On a lattice a single distance shell has no two adjacent vertices, so it \
spans no cycle and the family is empty. This is what a sphere of one-vertex \
thickness is on a lattice, not a defect of the definition."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f06b6154-5b49-4e60-b634-499b86df1e9e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Widening the radius to a band fixes it, and ",
 StyleBox["the band thickness that suffices tracks the girth of the tiling",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". On the square tiling, girth 4, the band ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d87f311b-8224-4213-87b8-d92aef2d948e"],
 " already carries a circle. On the hexagonal tiling, girth 6, it does not: \
the band has to reach ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", "+", " ", "2"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a747b053-90f9-4ab0-8ed3-81741056b40f"],
 ". On the triangular tiling, girth 3, a single shell carries a circle; on an \
irregular mesh it usually does, its vertices being adjacent by accident of \
the mesh."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"673a5396-239e-45b6-a1b5-cb2eed1d6f79"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its graph \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["circle", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<Graph\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7277f100-b9ec-4f19-be59-183d8727c812"],
 " \[LongDash] is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ddd2c1b-ce75-4fc1-bb91-a27df95473c5"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["atoms",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of the unrolled band. The band is cut along a radial seam, the band part \
of a shortest path from ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " to the nearest vertex outside the band, and unrolled: the circles through \
a seam vertex ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 " are the shortest paths of the cyclic cover of the band from ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 " to a second copy of ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 ". An atom is the DAG of those paths for one seam vertex, with the earlier \
seam vertices removed, so every circle lies in exactly one atom, at its first \
seam vertex. Only the atoms of least length are kept: an atom at a seam \
vertex that no shortest circle meets carries longer closed walks only. The \
atom is projected to the vertices of the graph, and its sink is kept as the \
separate vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "314503a2-82ab-4ed3-983d-7580a6c5e872"],
 ", a copy of its source ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 ". So the atom is acyclic, its chains from ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21327acb-ba6d-4d4f-9e58-1e796fe7c22a"],
 " are the circles read as closed walks, and its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Cardinality\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bfe85f2f-96c2-4d21-b2e1-2c8d6f654151"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Length\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c790c730-3b4c-4fff-a76d-e0c1b08c4653"],
 " are the chain count and the length of the circle."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f0966765-2809-4d7e-8722-4752a65fa388"],

Cell["\<\
The two sides of the seam are told apart by separation alone: two neighbours \
of a seam vertex lie on the same side iff the cycle through them and the cut \
band does not separate. No coordinates enter, and a circle may meet the seam \
any number of times.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"efcbe169-19c5-4f85-bdad-995092e6661e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The atoms need the cut band to be connected and the two sides to occur on \
the seam. Where the cut band is disconnected, or the seam has one side only, \
the graph is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "834d1ef0-5ec7-48f1-bf08-f73e1d7de370"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["necklaces",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " instead, cut from the band along the same seam: a DAG with one source ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 " and one sink, a copy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"s1", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ac930830-f6b9-4a9f-a802-abe8f3154277"],
 " of its source, again the cycle family opened at its closing arrow. A \
necklace needs the circle to meet the seam in one run, so it can miss a \
circle."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1a2e005a-ebb7-4414-9e3e-ff0afb3df570"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A member is a chain of the graph read as a cyclic vertex list: the copy of \
the source is dropped and the first vertex is not repeated. The ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Length\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fbd2d8dc-2936-4932-9789-250579118210"],
 " of a circle of ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " vertices is ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"283e9323-4e8c-49d4-8eea-1888c704c5ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The search.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["FindInfraRepresentative"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraRepresentative", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["circle", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c74e7221-cecf-4915-b7db-6f7463ed0a01"],
 " sweeps the band directly: for ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " = 3, 4, \[Ellipsis] it takes every cycle of length ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " of the band (",
 Cell[BoxData["FindCycle"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41424914-ec5b-4a27-ab6a-995e11a8e80f"],
 ") and keeps those whose removal leaves ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " in a component reaching no further than the band; the first ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " with a survivor gives the members. It does not read the graph, so it is \
the check on it, and it still answers where nothing lies beyond the band and \
separation is vacuous. Each length is enumerated in full before the filter, \
so the sweep is fast on a band one or two vertices thick and does not finish \
in reasonable time on a wide one, such as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "164cf926-6483-4c20-93a8-13c9f5acae06"],
 " on the square tiling."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9539a32b-c5e2-4121-9c29-b542296d6760"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every member separates. That the atoms carry every circle exactly once \
needs the winding functional, an invariant of the substrate that is nonzero \
exactly on the separating cycles, and a connected cut band; nothing here \
certifies the first. So ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1855c687-dcee-4e5c-b94a-941cb19414e8"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Undetermined"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/Undetermined", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "41e05b0f-05b8-4822-a5d6-8d93165164aa"],
 ", except that it is ",
 Cell[BoxData["False"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c98d16-bfef-4474-ae82-c96bd78f95a6"],
 " where the cut band is connected and the seam has one side only: there the \
winding functional or the annulus is witnessed to fail."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7a0df8ee-3365-4bd5-b5bc-7a7fbb06a6a5"],

Cell["Corresponding notions in the classical axiom systems:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0b9e7ef0-bcc7-476e-b30b-eab7058862a2"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "720afb85-d873-4895-a585-bb4401fa47f1"], Cell["System", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"16cb5414-2eb5-41f7-8acb-8015bcf37e13"],
